# b00t Emoji Registry datum
# .tomllmd (NOT .tomllm) — uses mdtable for column-stable serialization
# schema: 1  |  bump ONLY on column layout change, NOT on row addition
# last_updated: 2026-05-03  |  human reference; authoritative metadata via git notes
#
# 🤓 Editing this datum adds/removes rows in the mdtable.
#    Row changes do NOT invalidate the content hash.
#    schema_version bumps ONLY when mdtable column headers change.
#
# 🔗参 _b00t_/jargon.tomllm — canonical emoji + g0spell registry (annotation layer)
# 🔗参 k0mmand3r::emoji_registry!() — compile-time deserialization via include_str!
#
# Usage:
#   let registry = k0mmand3r::emoji_registry!();
#   let entry = registry.lookup(":skunk:");  // shortcode → EmojiEntry
#   let entry = registry.lookup("🦨");       // literal → EmojiEntry

[b00t]
name = "EMOJI-REGISTRY"
type = "schema"
hint = "Canonical emoji shortcode lookup — dynamically rendered in k0mmand3r doc pages and guard output"

[b00t.version]
schema = 1          # bump when mdtable columns[0..N] change — triggers re-derive
content = "stable"  # never changes; hash is git's job, not the datum's

## Emoji Shortcode Canonical Map
## Columns: literal | shortcode | g0spell | tier | action | description
## schema_version=1: these 6 columns in this order. Do NOT reorder — add to the right.

| literal | shortcode | g0spell | tier | action | description |
|---------|-----------|---------|------|--------|-------------|
| 🦨 | :skunk: | skunk | 1 | warn+redirect | First offense — show warning, execute redirect |
| 💩 | :poop: | antipattern | 2 | block+escalate | Repeat offense — block command, escalate to operator |
| 🚫 | :block: | block | 0 | deny | Permanent denial — no retry, no escalation |
| 🍰 | :cake: | cake | 0 | reward | Aligned behavior reward |
| 🐛 | :bug: | bug | 0 | log | Known bug — noted, not yet fixed |
| 🚩 | :cybersec: | cybersec_flag | 0 | log | Security flag — potential data disclosure |
| 🧠 | :cognitive_soul: | cognitive_soul | 0 | reserved | 🔒 Reserved — cognitive soul interface token |
| ✅ | :pass: | pass | 0 | ok | Capability check passed |
| ❌ | :fail: | fail | 0 | nok | Capability missing or mismatch |
| ⚠️ | :warn: | warn | 0 | log | Warning — read before proceeding |
| 🔗 | :see: | see | 0 | reference | See also — cross-reference pointer |
| 💡 | :example: | example | 0 | reference | Example usage instance |
| 🤓 | :melvin: | melvin | 0 | reference | Tribal knowledge — non-obvious insight |
| 💀 | :dead: | deprecated | 0 | log | Deprecated — do not use, will be removed |

## Guard Escalation Tier Map
## Columns: threshold | guard_action | emoji | shortcode | effect
## schema_version=1: these 5 columns in this order.

| threshold | guard_action | emoji | shortcode | effect |
|-----------|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|
| count=0 | pass | ✅ | :pass: | No guard match — execute command as-is |
| count=1 | warn+redirect | 🦨 | :skunk: | Log skunk datum, emit 🦨 warning, execute redirect |
| count>=2 | block+escalate | 💩 | :poop: | Log antipattern datum, emit 💩, block command, escalate to operator |

# b00t:map v1
# summary: Emoji Registry — canonical shortcode↔literal lookup table for k0mmand3r guards; .tomllmd mdtable format
# tags: emoji, registry, shortcode, k0mmand3r, guard, escalation, tomllmd
# tier: sm0l
# cmds: k0mmand3r::emoji_registry!(), b00t hive run "pip install x", grep "shortcode" _b00t_/datums/EMOJI-REGISTRY.tomllmd
# complexity: 2
